     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="method-section" id="time-difference" aria-labelledby="time-diff-heading">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Time Difference Mechanics</p>
    <h2 id="time-diff-heading">Analyzing the Time Gap: GMT vs IDT</h2>
    <p>
      The time difference between Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) and Israel Daylight Time (IDT) is exactly <strong>3 hours</strong>. Since GMT is fixed at UTC+0 and IDT operates at UTC+3, Israel runs three hours ahead of the meridian baseline. When it is 12:00 PM (Noon) in London during winter, local clocks in Tel Aviv and Jerusalem show 3:00 PM local time.
    </p>
    <p>
      This time difference shifts when standard winter time is active. From late October to late March, Israel switches to Israel Standard Time (IST, UTC+2), reducing the gap between Greenwich and Tel Aviv to 2 hours. This transition is designed to optimize daylight use during the summer months.
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Custom GMT vs IDT Timeline (SVG) -->
