        <text x="0" y="-17" font-family="'Manrope', sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="800" fill="#36c7b5" text-anchor="middle">+3 HOURS</text>
      </g>

      <g transform="translate(500, 100)">
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="60" fill="#12455d" stroke="#36c7b5" stroke-width="4" />
        <!-- IDT is +3 hours, so hands show 3:00 -->
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="30" y2="-30" stroke="#f4fbff" stroke-width="4" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="-45" stroke="#8fd7ff" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" />
        <circle cx="0" cy="0" r="5" fill="#36c7b5" />
        <text x="0" y="85" font-family="'Space Grotesk', sans-serif" font-weight="bold" font-size="16" fill="#f4fbff" text-anchor="middle">IDT Time (UTC+3)</text>
      </g>
    </svg>
  </div>

  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>GMT Reference Standard</h3>
      <p>Greenwich Mean Time (UTC+0) remains fixed year-round. It serves as the primary clock reference for databases, servers, and international aviation logs.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>Israel Summer Time (IDT)</h3>
      <p>Israel Daylight Time operates at UTC+3. It begins on the Friday before the last Sunday of March and ends on the last Sunday of October, maximizing summer evening light.</p>
    </article>
